Z||000000||FieroHarry||10-03-2001||11:13 PM||||During my trip home from RFTH6 I got stuck in a traffic jam, then completed a 1.5 hour run @ 85MPH.<BR>When I stopped for gas the fuel pump refused to start.<BR>Well needless to say after running around and getting another pump (thanks to some very friendly locals) and getting some blocks from more locals.<BR>I proceeded to jack the car up for a pump change out.<BR>Just before removing the tank (note it had sat for at least three hours) it decideds to run again.<BR>( I just had to check again before I committed to the change out).<P>So here two weeks later and driving her every day with no problems guess what happened today......<P>Thats right stuck in traffic for forty minutes or so. Stopped the car at grocery store one block from home and blammo, no fuel pump again after coming back out.<P>Two hours later its running again.<BR>I just changed this bastard last summer !<P>SO my question is this:<P>Could this be that my return line or relief valve in the regulator is shot?<BR>Seems to me the pump goes bad or not at all.<BR>For it to act like its over heating sounds like my return line is inop and causing the pump casing to get way to hot from no flow....<BR>Also note the bleeding of the fuel rail when this happens shows a mix of vaporized and liqued fuel.  NO THE PUMP CANNOT BE HEARD RUNNING and yes the voltage test shows its getting juice....&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<P>Any idea's you folks might have would help.<P>Thanks in advance.<P>So whats the concesus here, anybody ever heard of this one?<P>------------------<P><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||13
